{"id": "life-generations-cash-to-iou", "title": "A nursing-home chain’s homes moved $307.8 million of cash into related-company balances", "seconds": 127.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.072, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "4eb3f4d6307b0a57", "words": 418, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]", "trajectory"], "text": "314 million dollars.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 1.93, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$314.0 million", "label": "cash and securities, 27 California nursing homes", "sub": "end of 2024"}, "emph": ["314 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.48, 0.99, 1.31]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "That’s the cash 27 California nursing homes held at the end of 2024.", "t0": 2.05, "t1": 5.89, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$314.0 million", "label": "cash and securities, 27 California nursing homes", "sub": "end of 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.35, 0.63, 1.2, 1.76, 2.1, 2.35, 2.54, 2.63, 2.75, 2.9, 2.99, 3.28]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[1]", "amount"], "text": "A year later: 6.1 million.", "t0": 6.01, "t1": 7.97, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$6.1 million", "label": "the same 27 homes, end of 2025", "sub": "$307.8 million of cash moved"}, "emph": ["6.1 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.36, 0.83, 1.11, 1.4, 1.6]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "It’s a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 8.59, "t1": 9.87, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.31, 0.61, 0.77, 0.85]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "status"], "text": "Pooling cash with a parent company is common, and the homes still count it as theirs.", "t0": 9.99, "t1": 14.02, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.67, 0.81, 0.88, 1.17, 1.55, 1.67, 2.27, 2.47, 2.59, 2.87, 3.14, 3.38, 3.49, 3.61]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "actors[0]", "links[1]"], "text": "The first lead. All 27 homes name one parent: Life Generations Healthcare.", "t0": 14.24, "t1": 18.82, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Life Generations Healthcare", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "the parent named by 27 homes", "chip": "8 in the Bay Area, 1 in San Francisco"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.41, 1.03, 1.27, 1.82, 2.1, 2.33, 2.52, 3.2, 3.46, 4.06]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[0]"], "text": "As the cash went, what related companies owed the homes rose to 298.8 million.", "t0": 18.94, "t1": 23.86, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["cash, end of 2025", "$6.1 million"], "b": ["owed to the homes by related companies", "$298.8 million"]}, "emph": ["298.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.3, 0.6, 1.07, 1.28, 1.64, 2.1, 2.26, 2.38, 2.71, 2.94, 3.06, 3.3, 3.63, 4.1, 4.35, 4.55]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The homes’ net income that year: 53.6 million.", "t0": 23.98, "t1": 27.12, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["cash, end of 2025", "$6.1 million"], "b": ["owed to the homes by related companies", "$298.8 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.44, 0.62, 0.93, 1.12, 1.62, 2.21, 2.49, 2.77]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[3]", "innocent[5]"], "text": "But of the 335.1 million swing, 239.4 million is new money owed to homes.", "t0": 27.24, "t1": 34.1, "shot": "b5b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["new money owed to homes", "$239.4 million"], "b": ["debt the homes owed, paid down", "$95.7 million"], "kicker": "The $335.1 million swing"}, "emph": ["239.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.2, 0.31, 0.55, 0.82, 1.44, 1.73, 1.95, 2.31, 3.1, 3.32, 3.57, 4.13, 4.39, 4.65, 5.1, 5.4, 5.65, 6.03, 6.3, 6.43]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[3]"], "text": "And 95.7 million paid down what homes owed related companies.", "t0": 34.22, "t1": 37.72, "shot": "b5b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["new money owed to homes", "$239.4 million"], "b": ["debt the homes owed, paid down", "$95.7 million"], "kicker": "The $335.1 million swing"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.74, 0.99, 1.28, 1.64, 1.87, 2.07, 2.26, 2.54, 2.7, 3.03]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Why it matters: a home’s cash pays wages, food and repairs.", "t0": 37.84, "t1": 41.19, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A home’s cash pays wages, food and repairs."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.34, 0.99, 1.09, 1.37, 1.66, 1.95, 2.51, 2.77, 2.87]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Now the home depends on its owner’s other companies paying it back.", "t0": 41.31, "t1": 44.14, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A home’s cash pays wages, food and repairs."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.38, 0.59, 0.97, 1.08, 1.23, 1.52, 1.73, 2.13, 2.4, 2.5]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "actors[2]"], "text": "The second lead: four Bay Area homes. Cedar Crest, Plum Tree, Vista Manor, Pleasanton.", "t0": 44.36, "t1": 49.33, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Cash at the start of 2025, four Bay Area homes", "rows": [["Cedar Crest", "$36.0 million"], ["Plum Tree", "$35.2 million"], ["Vista Manor", "$34.9 million"], ["Pleasanton", "$31.5 million"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.42, 0.86, 1.11, 1.31, 1.64, 2.24, 2.55, 3.03, 3.32, 3.68, 4.0, 4.44]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "At 